# Mosquitto ACL for BrewHub (see README "MQTT ACLs").
#
# Model: the backend is the only client allowed to send commands
# (config/ota) to devices. Every device logs in with a username that is
# EXACTLY its DEVICE_ID, and may only touch its own unibrew/<id>/... topics.

# Backend: full access to BrewHub topics and Home Assistant discovery.
user brewhub-backend
topic readwrite unibrew/#
topic readwrite homeassistant/#

# Optional read-only consumer (e.g. Home Assistant). Uncomment and create
# the user with mosquitto_passwd if you need it.
# user homeassistant
# topic read unibrew/#
# topic read homeassistant/#

# Devices (pattern rules apply to every user, %u = MQTT username = DEVICE_ID).
pattern write unibrew/%u/status
pattern write unibrew/%u/telemetry
pattern write unibrew/%u/discovery
pattern write unibrew/%u/gravity
pattern read unibrew/%u/config
pattern read unibrew/%u/ota
